 2) Multiply the top and bottom of $9 \& 2$ by $\sqrt{9 \cdot 2 + 9}$. -Now for the common factor of 9 in $15\sqrt{9 \cdot 2 + 9}$, cancel it out. 3) Apply the same rule again and simplify. ... -to continue the process, multiply by $\sqrt{9-2}$ -to continue the process, multiply throughout by $\sqrt{9 \cdot 2 - 2}$ -to continue the process, multiply by $\sqrt{9 \cdot 2 + 9}$ -then simplify.
9&2
= \frac{\sqrt{9\cdot2+9}}{\sqrt{9\cdot2-2}}
& multiply top and bottom by $\sqrt{9\cdot2+9}=\sqrt{18+9}=\sqrt{27}$
=\frac{\sqrt{18}\cdot\sqrt{27}+\sqrt{18}\cdot9}{27-2}
= \frac{12\sqrt{3}+27}{25}

